---
import type { CasePart } from "../types";

interface Props {
  part: CasePart;
}
const { part } = Astro.props;
---

{part === "intro" && (
  <p>
    As a research assistant at Lifedu, I carried out the data analyses for a
    collaborative study combining an implicit association task,
    electroencephalography (EEG) and decision modeling.
  </p>
)}

{part === "visual" && (
  <figure class="portfolio-figure lifedu-workflow">
    <div class="portfolio-diagram lifedu-map">
      <div class="portfolio-node lifedu-context">
        <strong>Implicit association task</strong>
        <span>Community images and positive or negative words</span>
      </div>
      <div class="lifedu-streams">
        <section class="lifedu-stream" aria-labelledby="lifedu-behavior-route">
          <h2 id="lifedu-behavior-route">Behavioral observations</h2>
          <div class="portfolio-node">
            <strong>Response time</strong>
            <span>Correct or error choice</span>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="lifedu-stream" aria-labelledby="lifedu-eeg-route">
          <h2 id="lifedu-eeg-route">EEG recorded during the task</h2>
          <div class="portfolio-node">
            <strong>EEG recordings</strong>
          </div>
          <p class="lifedu-connection">
            <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          </p>
          <div class="portfolio-node">
            <strong>Preprocessing</strong>
          </div>
          <p class="lifedu-connection">
            <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          </p>
          <div class="portfolio-node">
            <strong>Trial-level CPP slope</strong>
            <span>CPP: centroparietal positivity</span>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
      <div class="portfolio-node lifedu-matching">
        <strong>Matched trials</strong>
        <span>Link each CPP slope to its corresponding behavioral trial</span>
      </div>
      <div class="lifedu-inputs">
        <div class="portfolio-node">
          <strong>Fitting observations</strong>
          <span>Response times + correct/error choices</span>
        </div>
        <div class="portfolio-node">
          <strong>Drift-rate specification</strong>
          <span>CPP slope enters as a measured covariate</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="lifedu-connection">
        Together inform <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
      </p>
      <div class="portfolio-node lifedu-fit">
        <strong>Fit candidate models</strong>
      </div>
      <p class="lifedu-connection">
        <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
      </p>
      <div class="portfolio-node lifedu-compare">
        <strong>Compare candidate explanations</strong>
        <span>Fit and complexity</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      Analysis workflow: behavioral responses inform model fitting, while a
      derived EEG measure enters the drift-rate specification.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
)}

{part === "body" && (
  <>
    <p>
      Participants classified community images and positive or negative words.
      “Own” meant their residential community; “other” meant another community.
      Across two response mappings, the community category sharing a key with
      positive words changed.
    </p>

    <figure class="portfolio-figure lifedu-task">
      <div class="portfolio-diagram lifedu-mappings">
        <section aria-labelledby="lifedu-mapping-one">
          <h3 id="lifedu-mapping-one">Mapping 1</h3>
          <dl>
            <div>
              <dt>Response A</dt>
              <dd>Own community + positive words</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Response B</dt>
              <dd>Other community + negative words</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="lifedu-mapping-two">
          <h3 id="lifedu-mapping-two">Mapping 2</h3>
          <dl>
            <div>
              <dt>Response A</dt>
              <dd>Own community + negative words</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Response B</dt>
              <dd>Other community + positive words</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        The two category mappings used counterbalanced response keys. Images and
        words were classified successively, each remaining on screen until a
        response.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>Connecting measurements and models</h2>
    <p>
      I preprocessed the EEG recordings and extracted slopes of centroparietal
      positivity (CPP), then matched valid EEG measures with the corresponding
      behavioral trials.
    </p>
    <p>
      I fitted drift diffusion models to response times and correct or incorrect
      choices. Drift rate represents the model’s rate of evidence accumulation.
      In joint EEG–behavior models, trial-level CPP slopes entered the
      drift-rate specification.
    </p>
    <h2>Keeping valid error responses</h2>
    <p>
      In this study, error trials were excluded from response-time summaries,
      while valid error responses were retained as choice information for
      decision modeling. The model needed the pattern of correct and incorrect
      responses as well as their timing.
    </p>

    <details class="portfolio-methods">
      <summary>Model fitting and comparison</summary>
      <p>
        Models were fitted using aggregate maximum-likelihood estimation in
        PyDDM. I compared candidate specifications using BIC, considering fit
        alongside model complexity. CPP slope entered the drift-rate
        specification as a measured covariate; the resulting drift rate was a
        model parameter.
      </p>
    </details>
  </>
)}

<style>
  .lifedu-workflow {
    max-width: 56rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .lifedu-map {
    padding: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }
  .lifedu-map .portfolio-node {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .lifedu-context,
  .lifedu-matching,
  .lifedu-fit,
  .lifedu-compare {
    text-align: center;
  }
  .lifedu-context {
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .lifedu-streams,
  .lifedu-inputs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }
  .lifedu-stream {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .lifedu-stream h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--portfolio-muted);
  }
  .lifedu-matching {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    border-style: dashed;
  }
  .lifedu-connection {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin: 0.4rem 0;
    color: var(--portfolio-muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
  .lifedu-connection span {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--portfolio-accent);
  }
  .lifedu-inputs + .lifedu-connection {
    margin: 0.8rem 0;
  }
  .lifedu-fit,
  .lifedu-compare {
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .lifedu-compare {
    border-color: var(--portfolio-accent);
  }
  .lifedu-mappings {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }
  .lifedu-mappings section {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .lifedu-mappings h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .lifedu-mappings dl {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .lifedu-mappings dl > div {
    padding-block: 0.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
  }
  .lifedu-mappings dt {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    color: var(--portfolio-accent);
  }
  .lifedu-mappings dd {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--portfolio-ink);
  }
  @media (max-width: 539px) {
    .lifedu-map,
    .lifedu-map .portfolio-node,
    .lifedu-mappings {
      padding: 12px;
    }
    .lifedu-streams,
    .lifedu-inputs,
    .lifedu-mappings {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .lifedu-stream + .lifedu-stream {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
      padding-top: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
